 [['Tyrosine —TH→ L-DOPA is the rate-limiting step.','L-DOPA —AADC/DDC→ dopamine.','Dopamine —DBH→ norepinephrine.','Norepinephrine —PNMT→ epinephrine.','DBH blockade reduces NE and downstream synthesis; upstream dopamine may accumulate in the simplified model.'],'Do not omit L-DOPA in diagrams or prose. Distinguish tyrosine from tryptophan hydroxylase.'],
 [['5-HT follows tryptophan → 5-HTP → 5-HT through TPH and AADC.','DA follows tyrosine → L-DOPA → DA through TH and AADC.','Distinguish TPH from TH; tryptophan availability influences 5-HT synthesis, while TH is the classical catecholamine rate-limiting enzyme.','Corresponding Na⁺-dependent plasma-membrane transporters mediate uptake.','MAO metabolizes monoamines; catecholamine metabolism can also involve COMT. Clearance differs from synthesis.'],'Classroom substrate emphasis and textbook rate-limiting reactions can coexist. ACh is not a monoamine in this comparison.'],
 [['GAD decarboxylates glutamate to form GABA.','GAD inhibition usually reduces GABA synthesis.','GABA transaminase participates in breakdown; inhibiting it reduces GABA metabolism.','In mature circuits, GABA commonly lowers spike probability through GABA_A/GABA_B pathways.','Losing GABAergic cells generally reduces inhibition and increases excitability; state the circuit assumptions.'],'Do not predict reduced transmitter for both synthetic-enzyme inhibition and degradation-enzyme inhibition.'],
 [['Synthetic-enzyme inhibition reduces new supply; existing stores can delay the effect.','Loading inhibition reduces releasable vesicular content without necessarily removing cytoplasmic transmitter.','Plasma-membrane reuptake inhibition usually prolongs extracellular exposure.','Receptor antagonism reduces receptor activation at the same transmitter concentration.','Separate action sites, hold other conditions fixed and avoid identifying one mechanism from phenotype alone.'],'More extracellular transmitter does not prove direct agonism. Reduced synthesis need not immediately empty vesicles.'],
 [['Record the same postsynaptic cell under matched control and drug conditions.','Compare presynaptic stimulation with direct local application of the normal transmitter.','A preserved direct response supports functioning receptors/downstream signaling and an upstream excitation or release defect.','If direct application also fails, consider receptors/downstream pathways, dose and viability before localizing uniquely.','Add presynaptic AP/Ca²⁺ or release measurements to refine localization and state inference limits.'],'Rescue locates the range of bypassed steps, not one unique molecule. Keep matched controls.']
